34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems that ""perfect fairness"" often comes with a heavy administrative tax. I've seen a house that meters everything, and it's a tedious monthly ritual.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,Oh no! I saw that too! Forty minutes every month just for the readings? And the template looked like a total nightmare to fill out. We can't do that!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found that some rooms use four times more energy than others. If we keep splitting equally, the low-users are definitely subsidizing the high-users. That's where the resentment comes from.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The monthly variance is alarming. The winter bills are nearly triple the summer ones. It's impossible to budget when the cost swings so wildly from month to month.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I saw the payment log. People get really upset when the amount changes suddenly or when they are reminded late. It's not just about the money, it's the feeling.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, while the disparity is real, we must ask: is the cost of measuring it worth the social friction? I'd rather we be warm and happy than precise and miserable.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! @Benjamin is right! If we spend an hour every month fighting over a few dollars, we're losing our free time. We need something fast and easy!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"But @Benjamin, ignoring the disparity doesn't make it go away; it just hides it. The resentment is already there. Objective data is the only way to clear the air.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,I'm also concerned about the cost of precision. I've seen that installing sub-meters would be incredibly expensive up front. We can't afford a huge initial fee.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I agree with @Victoria. I think the ""reminders"" are what hurt the most. When someone asks for money, it feels like they are saying ""you are lazy"" or ""you are wrong.""","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I suspect that if we make the system too rigid, we'll all start sitting in our coats to save a few cents. That's a psychological price I'm not willing to pay.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Right! Imagine us all shivering just to avoid a ""high usage"" label! That's not a home, that's a competition. Let's pick a way that takes five minutes, not fifty.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I'm not suggesting we live in the dark, but we should acknowledge that some of us use far more. A system that reflects usage would actually be the kindest approach.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we can't afford the meters, maybe we can find a middle ground. But we must address the winter spikes. A flat monthly average would be much more stable for us.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"Maybe we can find a way to pay that doesn't require someone to be the ""collector""? If the system is automatic, maybe we won't feel like we're accusing each other.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are torn between the precision of the accountant and the peace of the poet. I believe a system that prioritizes comfort and simplicity will serve us best.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,Yes! Let's go for the one that's the least amount of work! I'm voting for whatever doesn't involve a spreadsheet that takes an hour to fill out!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I still believe that transparency is the only cure for the rumors of unfairness. I will support any option that ties the cost to the actual energy consumed.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I will support a system that provides financial predictability. I cannot handle another winter where the utility bill feels like a second rent payment.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want us to stop being mean to each other. If a system removes the need for ""reminders,"" I think that's the best one for our hearts.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
