60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is a recipe for a cold house and a tense atmosphere. I'll be voting against it to ensure we don't start counting every lightbulb we switch on.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh, definitely not C! I saw how long that takes at the other house! It's way too much work. I'm leaning towards A because it's the simplest!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C is the only one that addresses the actual disparity in usage. If we want to stop the rumors of people ""carrying"" others, we need to see the numbers.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is financially unfeasible due to the installation costs. Between A and B, Option B is far superior because it prevents those sudden, stressful winter spikes.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option C sounds like it would make us watch each other even more. I don't like the idea of us monitoring each other's electricity.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I agree that predictability is a virtue. Option B allows us to enjoy the winter without the guilt of a ticking meter, which is a significant psychological win.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"Wait, @Victoria, does Option B mean we still have to do a big calculation at the end of the year? Because that sounds like a lot of work for one person!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the ""guilt"" you mention is exactly what I'm talking about. People feel guilt or resentment because the system is opaque. Option C makes it transparent.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, a single annual reconciliation is a small price to pay for twelve months of budget stability. It's much better than the current chaos of the utility envelope.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A is okay, but the amount changes every month. I saw in the logs that when the amount changes, people start to argue.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, @Minato. Option B smooths out the emotional and financial peaks. It treats the house as a collective experience rather than a series of individual transactions.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"Hmm, if it's just once a year, I guess I can handle that. But Option A is still the fastest! No calculations at all, just divide by five and you're done!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I cannot in good conscience vote for A or B. They both ignore the fact that some of us are paying for others' luxury. Fairness requires measurement.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,Fairness is irrelevant if the system is unaffordable or creates financial instability. Option B is the only rational choice for someone who needs to plan their monthly budget.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Option B is the gentlest. If the price stays the same for a few months, we won't have to send as many reminders or feel like we're accusing anyone.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have a consensus on the desire for peace and predictability. I'll cast my vote for the system that protects our comfort and our friendship.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm still worried about the work, but if @Minato and @Victoria think B is better for the mood, I'll go with that. Let's just make sure the year-end part is easy!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I will stand by my preference for C. I believe that true peace comes from honesty and objective fairness, not from ignoring the problem under a blanket of ""simplicity.""","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I've analyzed the costs and the volatility. Option B is the only sustainable path that avoids high upfront fees while ensuring we aren't blindsided by winter costs.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm voting for B. I want us to be able to talk to each other about things other than money. I hope this makes our home feel warmer.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
